Honour $(CC), $(CFLAGS) and $(LDFLAGS) in the Makefile.

Upstream hardcodes gcc and passes neither CFLAGS nor LDFLAGS, so the build
cannot be pointed at conda's compiler or at zlib under $PREFIX. That breaks
the osx (clang) build and the cross-compiled linux-aarch64 / osx-arm64
builds outright, and is not specific to conda -- any packager installing
zlib outside the system prefix hits it.

$(CC) defaults to cc in GNU make and both flag variables default to empty,
so a plain "make" in a normal checkout builds exactly as it does today.

Reported upstream at:
https://github.com/jsh58/Genrich/issues/102#issuecomment-5513399276

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
index 03b388e..946a94d 100644
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -1,2 +1,2 @@
 Genrich: Genrich.c Genrich.h
-	gcc -g -Wall -std=gnu99 -O2 -o Genrich Genrich.c -lz -lm
+	$(CC) -g -Wall -std=gnu99 $(LDFLAGS) $(CFLAGS) -O2 -o Genrich Genrich.c -lz -lm
